{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790345302,"nonce":"0D/M2J6e0A/E7rVbBOt9AZw1hm4=","title":"Lua: _G.name does not make _ENV an upvalue","message":"A function that reaches a global only as _G.name (read or assigned) has no _ENV upvalue in zylua: scope.rs global_table_member binds _G without a lookup, so Upvalue::Env is never pushed. Lua numbers _ENV where _G is first mentioned.\n\nReproducer:\n\n    local p = 1\n    local function f() return _G.x, p end\n    print(debug.getupvalue(f, 1), debug.getupvalue(f, 2))\n\nlua5.4 prints _ENV and p; zylua prints p and nothing. A string.dump of f still runs correctly (the loaded copy reaches _G through its chunk environment), but getupvalue and setupvalue on it see the wrong numbering.\n\nFound while building string.dump (LO-string-dump).","files":null}]}